WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Hey, how's it goin', bros? My name is PewDiePie!

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.820
Today is a very… Special… Day. Lemme tell you why.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.820
We're playing Mirror's Edge™ 2

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.940
or Cataclyst…?

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:10.820
Catalyst.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.260
Whatever, no one cares.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.820
Mirror's Edge™ 2. I'll just call it that.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.180
Uh, a lot of people don't know this,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.360
but Mirror's Edge™ was one of the first games

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.820
I ever recorded for my YouTube channel.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.820
It was on my first channel, which

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.820
was YouTube.com/PewDie

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.820
which I forgot the password to

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.420
and created PewDiePie. So I

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.820
used to upload videos playing that game and

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.820
I remember people were just obsessed with this game.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.820
They wanted a sequel and here we

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.820
are, six– What is it? Six

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.820
years later? We finally got one.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.820
Uh, I don't know why it took them so

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.700
long, but… For me

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.820
Mirror's Edge™ is an amazing game

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.820
because of the gameplay. DICE™,

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.820
the company that made this game, they really do first

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.820
person experiences better than no other,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.820
and uh,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.820
a lot of games…

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.820
do it these days, but back in the day,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.820
what they did with Mirror's Edge™ was

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.820
uh, was really innovative and really

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.820
uh… Pushing– Pushing

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.820
uh, new limits and

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.820
I, uh, I'm curious to see if they're

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.820
gonna do the same with this title. The only

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.820
thing that was really bad about the first game was the

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.820
story, and it looks like they're trying to tell

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.820
a better story this time, so… I'm really

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.820
excited to go on a new adventure with you bros! Especially

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.820
a game that I have a personal

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.820
uh, connection to, I guess you can

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.820
say and– and to share that online with

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.820
y'all, I think is really cool.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.820
And I'm really excited to do this.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.820
Uh… To play one of the games

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.820
that I started playing.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.820
Will it be good? I sure

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.820
